@yusukebe 
Sorry for the late reply! I think the overall direction makes sense.
I found a few things that could use fixes, so I opened a follow-up PR: [#5536](https://github.com/honojs/hono/pull/5536). Could you merge it into this branch, or cherry-pick whichever commits you think are needed?

Hi @yusukebe

Yeah, I think we’re good to go with this patch.

Just to double-check, if the request contains invalid UTF-8, calling `text()` before `arrayBuffer()` can still change the body bytes, as in the example below. Are we okay with treating this as known behavior?

```ts
import { Hono } from './src/index'

const app = new Hono()

app.post('/', async (c) => {
  await c.req.text()
  return c.json([...new Uint8Array(await c.req.arrayBuffer())])
})

const res = await app.request('/', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/plain; charset=utf-8' },
  body: new Uint8Array([0xff, 0x00, 0x41]),
})

// Invalid UTF-8: FF becomes EF BF BD.
console.log(await res.json())
// [239, 191, 189, 0, 65]
```
